Unlockupd works around a bug in lookupd, a system service in Mac OS X 10.0 - 10.4 which is required for proper operation of Mac OS X. If lookupd fails, the system quickly becomes unusable. Unlockupd periodically checks lookupd's status and forces it to restart should it fail.\
\
Mac OS X 10.5 (Leopard) appears to have fixed the problem by eliminating lookupd altogether. Installing Unlockupd on Leopard should cause no problems, but it is not recommended, as it is not necessary.\
\
This installer guides you through the steps necessary to install unlockupd. To get started, click Continue.\
